{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1125373-the-five-families-of-venice","id":1125373,"title":"The five families of Venice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T15:08:38-07:00","id":1125373,"title":"The five families of Venice","content":"So, i'm starting a game set in Venice in 1204-1205 (shortly after the sack of constantinople) and part of the kindred political landscape is a grouping of 5 (so far) important bloodlines that have influence within the aristocracy of Venice and that sets themselves as protector of the kindred society. Them and another group (the guilds) will form in essence the invictus (with the lancea sanctum being the other major group in the city).<br /> This is what i have thought of so far. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> The short and sweet: I made 5 bloodlines (mostly taken from existing bloodlines with a few tweeks) for my 1200s Venice setting. I'm having a bit of a difficulty with the daeva bloodline as i have a few ideas but i cant see how to make them fit together. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Grimani family (Gangrel)<br /> <br /> I had a lot of problem initially thinking of an appropriate gangrel bloodline so i asked a little help in the forum and found out i had completely forgotten about the Kerberos bloodline which proved to be pretty much exactly what i was searching for. The only thing i'm thinking of changing would be switching the extra discipline of majesty for nightmare. I'm going to have the leader of the bloodline be the official leader of the five families (and by extension the Prince of the city) and i kind of want him/her and the bloodline to be more feared than well liked. So in that sense i feel that nightmare is more appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Morosini family (mekhet)<br /> <br /> I've had a lot of idea for the mekhet family. Obviously i've been inspired by the sangiovanni bloodline except that i want to move away from the corpse raising aspect of necromancy to focuse more on ghosts. I'm giving them Dominate as the fourth discipline. The thing that inspired me most about the sangiovanni bloodline (and its spiritual predecessor in Mascarade) is having the mortal family be strongly intertwinned with the kindred part of it. Therefore i want the family to also have a strong focus on necromancy. I'm not thinking of having awakened member in the family but definitely a fair number of mortal with the medium merit and a good knowledge of rituals to summon, bind/ward and exorcise ghosts.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking on (definitely not sure about that tho) doing a bit of an switch on expectations by having the mortal side know about the kindred in their midst but also be in control of them. With having members of the family becoming kindred be a decision of the family. I'm toying with the idea that the real leader of the family be some sort of geist or an ancestor ghost that keeps claiming a mortal member of the family every generation. Of course none of this is knows by the greater kindred society and its a very closely guarded secret of the bloodline. <br /> <br /> So far i'm thinking of having the bloodline curse be that it cost more blood to have the blush of life. But i feel its a bit boring and i'd like a curse that have to do with ghosts somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Marcello family (ventrue)<br /> <br /> The Marcello family will be the Marcellarius bloodline (one of my favorites bloodline) and i'm giving them vigor as the fourth discipline. Aside from that i'm not changing anything. For the story i'm having them be the ones who want to be in power and i'm looking forward to use quotes of the baron harkonnen from dune (i dont remember the wording but something to do with a leader being the biggest predator who must always be more hungry and never be sated).<br /> <br /> <br /> The Baddacelli family(nosferatu)<br /> <br /> The Baddacelli family was easier to make as i took the baddacelli bloodline of nosferatu that loses its eyesight and gain the capacity to mimic and project any sound. I am changing them a bit tho in that i am giving them majesty as the fourth discipline. The idea here is i am making the baddacelli into masters of ambiance either alluring or terrifying. As this is a game that will see the players go through the centuries, I want the player to meet the family again but this time the bloodline will be more like the book depict them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Foscari family (daeva)<br /> <br /> I am having a bit of difficulties with that one. There are many ideas which i am trying to fit together and i'm not sure i'm succeeding. <br /> The idea i had is that the family out of boredom and a taste for taboos started learning and practicing blood magic (cruac). Most members of the bloodline know at least one cruac ritual and they are willing to teach to vampires outside the bloodline that wishes to participate in the ceremonies. That way, if one of my players wishes to learn cruac there is a possibility. <br /> In essence i am imagining them as a crone cult hiding in the middle of high society. <br /> <br /> Honestly i think the bloodline that fit best is the Duchagne. But the thing is that i kind of wanted to give the bloodline obfuscate as an extra discipline (to represent them doing forbidden ceremonies in secrets) and finding a way to theme it somehow with mask wearing. I think there is an interesting symbology between mask and venice but i'm not sure how to incorporate that in an interesting bloodline.<br /> <br /> Essentially what do you think would be an interesting bloodline curse and bloodline gift that fits the elements i've set up for the family (namely; practicing cruac tho doesnt mind teaching it to others, obfuscate as the fourth discipline and masks)? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T10:35:03-07:00","id":1125950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1125373-the-five-families-of-venice#post1125373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Morosini family (mekhet)<br /> <br /> I've had a lot of idea for the mekhet family. Obviously i've been inspired by the sangiovanni bloodline except that i want to move away from the corpse raising aspect of necromancy to focuse more on ghosts. I'm giving them Dominate as the fourth discipline. The thing that inspired me most about the sangiovanni bloodline (and its spiritual predecessor in Mascarade) is having the mortal family be strongly intertwinned with the kindred part of it. Therefore i want the family to also have a strong focus on necromancy. I'm not thinking of having awakened member in the family but definitely a fair number of mortal with the medium merit and a good knowledge of rituals to summon, bind/ward and exorcise ghosts.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking on (definitely not sure about that tho) doing a bit of an switch on expectations by having the mortal side know about the kindred in their midst but also be in control of them. With having members of the family becoming kindred be a decision of the family. I'm toying with the idea that the real leader of the family be some sort of geist or an ancestor ghost that keeps claiming a mortal member of the family every generation. Of course none of this is knows by the greater kindred society and its a very closely guarded secret of the bloodline.<br /> <br /> So far i'm thinking of having the bloodline curse be that it cost more blood to have the blush of life. But i feel its a bit boring and i'd like a curse that have to do with ghosts somehow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I used these guys as an inspiration for a Mekhet bloodline that deals with ghosts:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline\"> The Stygians (fan bloodline) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Stygians They told me it was a Gift from God. I&rsquo;m not so sure anymore. The Stygians are an unusual bloodline and often considered eccentric by their </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T10:56:04-07:00","id":1125959,"title":"","content":"The Morosini could be strongly mercantile, which fits both Venice and the death and physicality intersect a lot in the ChroD setting (from the Moros Arcana to the feel of the Underworld, to a Sineater's bling to vampires' feeding on blood). They bought their first members' embraces with a stack of cash. A curse might be that they have to trade for their blood - leave a physical token of some sort behind when they feed - though I don't really like that one. Maybe feeding infects them with compulsions based on their victim's vice(s) - just for a night or two if the victim survives, permanent if they die - or for more of a weakness, a full-on hostile spirit that bedevils them like a Hollow Mekhet's ka.<br /> <br /> The Badacellis sound like they'd be involved in the Carnivale, big time.<br /> <br /> As for the Foscari... Their faces changing on their Embraces, to make it impossible to continue their former lives (representing masks and initiation) could be a gift or curse depending on the circumstances - but probably not enough to be the Bloodline Gift or Curse, just some interesting atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:43:23-07:00","id":1126304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1125373-the-five-families-of-venice?p=1125950#post1125950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used these guys as an inspiration for a Mekhet bloodline that deals with ghosts:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-fan-bloodline</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting. I like the bloodline curse of having to sleep in a place close to death. I was trying something involving being haunted but it felt a bit to involved a curse for a group of npcs. This is much more manageable while still being very evocative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1125373-the-five-families-of-venice?p=1125959#post1125959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the Foscari... Their faces changing on their Embraces, to make it impossible to continue their former lives (representing masks and initiation) could be a gift or curse depending on the circumstances - but probably not enough to be the Bloodline Gift or Curse, just some interesting atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. I think you put your finger on something i wasnt able to fully articulate with the family in that it makes them more inclusive than the other four. I was planning for the Morosini to be the least inclusive (as in only accept member of the mortal family for the bloodline) but i wanted the foscari to be different. If you renounce your old life when you join the bloodline it feels like they would accept kindred more easily into the bloodline. I mean it matters less who you were before.<br /> As for the curse, i'm thinking you lose all social merit (not the point as per the sanctity of merit thing) but i'm thinking it could be a bit to harsh???<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:54:15-07:00","id":1126309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1125373-the-five-families-of-venice?p=1126304#post1126304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting. I like the bloodline curse of having to sleep in a place close to death. I was trying something involving being haunted but it felt a bit to involved a curse for a group of npcs. This is much more manageable while still being very evocative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}